' =============================================================================
' OBSERVER (backend)
' =============================================================================
@startuml pattern_observer
title Observer — car listing changes notify renters who watch a car

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "patterns.observer" {
  class CarSubject <<Subject>> {
    - _observers : List
    + attach(observer)
    + detach(observer)
    + detach_by_user(user_id)
    + notify(car_data, change_type)
  }

  class WatcherObserver <<Observer>> {
    + user_id
    + max_price, desired_start, desired_end
    + callback
    + update(car_data, change_type)
  }

  class WatchManager {
    - _subjects : Map<car_id, CarSubject>
    + get_or_create_subject(car_id)
    + add_watcher(car_id, observer)
    + remove_watcher(car_id, user_id)
    + notify_car_change(car_id, car_data, change_type)
  }
}

package "services" {
  class "car_service\n(module)" as car_service_mod {
    .. global ..
    **watch_manager** : WatchManager
    --
    + update_listing(...)  '' calls notify on price/availability
  }

  class "watch_service\n(module)" as watch_service_mod {
    + watch_car(user_id, car_id, ...)
    + unwatch_car(...)
    + restore_watchers()
  }
}

package "services.notification_service" {
  class "add_notification(...)" as add_notif <<callback target>>
}

WatchManager "1" o-- "0..*" CarSubject : manages
CarSubject "1" o-- "0..*" WatcherObserver : notifies

watch_service_mod ..> WatcherObserver : **creates** (with callback)
watch_service_mod ..> car_service_mod : **imports** watch_manager
WatcherObserver ..> add_notif : **callback**(user_id, message)\nfrom _make_callback()

note right of CarSubject
  **Mapping**
  **Subject** → **CarSubject** (one per watched car_id).
  **Observer** → **WatcherObserver** (one per user watching that car).
  **ConcreteSubject** is not a separate class; **WatchManager**
  holds **CarSubject** instances keyed by car id.
end note

note bottom of watch_service_mod
  **Persistence**: watcher criteria stored on **cars.json**;
  **restore_watchers()** rebuilds **WatcherObserver** instances on startup.
end note

@enduml


' =============================================================================
' MEDIATOR (frontend)
' =============================================================================
@startuml pattern_mediator
title Mediator — UI components communicate via DriveShareMediator

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "frontend/src/patterns/mediator.js" {
  class Colleague <<Colleague (abstract)>> {
    # name : string
    # mediator : DriveShareMediator
    + send(event, data)
    + receive(event, data)
  }

  class DriveShareMediator <<ConcreteMediator>> {
    - _colleagues : Map<name, Colleague>
    - _eventLog
    + register(colleague)
    + unregister(name)
    + notify(senderName, event, data)
    + getEventLog()
  }

  note right of DriveShareMediator
    **EVENTS** and **ROUTING_TABLE** live in the same module:
    each event maps to colleague **names** that should **receive** it.
    **USER_LOGGED_OUT** broadcasts to all registered colleagues.
  end note
}

package "frontend/src/hooks/useColleague.js" {
  class ComponentColleague <<ConcreteColleague>> {
    - _handler
    + receive(event, data)
  }
}

package "frontend/src/context/MediatorContext.jsx" {
  class "MediatorProvider / useMediator()" as MediatorCtx
}

Colleague <|-- ComponentColleague
ComponentColleague --> DriveShareMediator : mediator.notify(...)
DriveShareMediator ..> Colleague : routes to **receive()**

MediatorCtx ..> DriveShareMediator : provides singleton\nmediator to tree

note as NCol
  **Concrete colleague instances (string names in code)**
  Registered via **useColleague('Name', handler)** — names must match
  **ROUTING_TABLE** keys where that component should receive events.
  --
  **Receivers / senders (examples)**:
  **NotificationBell**, **BalanceDisplay**, **CarList**, **WatchList**,
  **BookingList**, **ConversationList**, **MyCarsOwnerList**;
  event-only senders include **PaymentButton**, **BookingModal**, **CarForm**,
  **ChatWindow**, **ReviewForm** (they still use **useColleague** to **send**).
end note

ComponentColleague .. NCol

@enduml


' =============================================================================
' CHAIN OF RESPONSIBILITY (backend)
' =============================================================================
@startuml pattern_chain_of_responsibility
title Chain of Responsibility — password recovery security questions

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "patterns.chain_of_responsibility" {
  class SecurityQuestionHandler <<Handler>> {
    - _question_index : int
    - _next_handler : SecurityQuestionHandler
    + set_next(handler) : Handler
    + handle(user, answers) : bool
  }
}

package "patterns.chain_of_responsibility" as factory {
  class "build_security_chain()" as build_chain <<factory>> {
    returns first handler in chain
  }
}

package "services.auth_service" {
  class "recover_password(email, answers, new_password)" as recover_pw {
    uses **build_security_chain()**
    then **chain.handle(user, answers)**
  }
}

SecurityQuestionHandler "1" --> "0..1" SecurityQuestionHandler : _next_handler
build_chain ..> SecurityQuestionHandler : **chains** handler[0]→[1]→[2]
recover_pw ..> build_chain : **calls**

note bottom of SecurityQuestionHandler
  **Mapping**
  **Handler** → **SecurityQuestionHandler** (one link per question index).
  **successor** → **set_next** / **_next_handler**.
  Client → **auth_service.recover_password** starts the chain via **build_security_chain()**.
end note

@enduml


' =============================================================================
' PROXY (backend)
' =============================================================================
@startuml pattern_proxy
title Proxy — payment validation, logging, delegation

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "patterns.proxy" {
  class RealPaymentService <<RealSubject>> {
    + process(renter_id, owner_id, amount)
  }

  class PaymentProxy <<Proxy>> {
    - _real_service : RealPaymentService
    - _transaction_log
    + process_payment(renter_id, owner_id, amount, booking_id?)
    + get_transaction_log()
    - _log_transaction(...)
  }
}

package "services.payment_service" {
  class "process_payment(...)" as pay_svc <<Client API>> {
    delegates to module-level\n**_payment_proxy**
  }
}

PaymentProxy o-- RealPaymentService : delegates **process()**
pay_svc ..> PaymentProxy : **process_payment()**

note right of PaymentProxy
  **Proxy responsibilities** (actual code):
  validate amount & balance → delegate **RealPaymentService.process** →
  log transaction → on success create **notifications** and optional **booking** paid flag.
end note

@enduml


' =============================================================================
' SINGLETON (backend)
' =============================================================================
@startuml pattern_singleton
title Singleton — single SessionManager for current user session

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "patterns.singleton" {
  class SessionManager <<Singleton>> {
    {static} _instance
    + login(user)
    + logout()
    + get_current_user()
    + is_authenticated()
    + update_user(updates)
    + refresh()
    {static} reset()
  }
}

package "Integration" {
  class "auth_service.login / logout / ..." as auth_int
  class "api.routes.auth (SessionManager)" as api_auth
}

SessionManager <-- auth_int : **SessionManager()**
SessionManager <-- api_auth : **SessionManager()**

note right of SessionManager
  **__new__** ensures a single instance; all callers share **\_current_user**.
end note

@enduml


' =============================================================================
' BUILDER (backend)
' =============================================================================
@startuml pattern_builder
title Builder — stepwise construction of car listing dict

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package "patterns.builder" {
  class CarListingBuilder <<Builder>> {
    + set_owner(owner_id)
    + set_make / set_model / set_year / ...
    + add_feature(feature)
    + add_availability(start, end)
    + validate()
    + build() : car dict
  }
}

package "models.car" {
  class "create_car(...)" as create_car <<Product factory>> {
    returns listing **dict**
  }
}

package "api.routes.cars" {
  class "POST /cars create_listing" as create_route {
    instantiates **CarListingBuilder**,\nfluent calls,\n**build()**
  }
}

package "services.car_service" {
  class "create_listing(car_data)" as car_create_svc {
    persists dict to **cars.json**
  }
}

CarListingBuilder ..> create_car : **build()** calls
create_route ..> CarListingBuilder : **uses**
create_route ..> car_create_svc : **create_listing**(built dict)

note right of CarListingBuilder
  **Mapping**
  **Builder** → **CarListingBuilder**
  **Product** → car listing **dict** from **create_car** (not a separate class).
  **Director** is not implemented; **api/routes/cars.py** orchestrates steps.
end note

@enduml
